      "text": "To find the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and express it in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials, but extended to polynomials).\n\nFirst, let's distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, let's perform each multiplication:\n\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot 7 = 21x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) = -6x^3\n\\]\n\\[\n(-5x) \\cdot 7 = -35x\n\\]\n\\[\n(-5x) \\cdot (-2x) = 10x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 7 = 28\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\cdot (-2x) = -8x\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine all these terms:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 21x^2 + 10x^2 - 35x - 8x + 28\n\\]\n\nNow, combine the like terms:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nSo, the polynomial \\(3x^2 - 5x + 4\\) in the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\) is:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nThus, we identify the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\\[\n28 = 28\n\\]\n\nNow, sum these values:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nPerform the addition and subtraction step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 = 76\n\\]\n\\[\n76 - 86 = -10\n\\]\n\\[\n-10 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
