      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "First, let's expand the expression $(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)$ using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials).\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) - 5x \\cdot 7 - 5x \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nSimplify each term:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nNow, we have the expanded form $-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28$. By comparing it with the form $ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d$, we identify the coefficients:\n\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of $8a + 4b + 2c + d$. Substitute the values of $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ into the expression:\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n= -48 + 124 - 86 + 28\n\\]\n\nCombine the results:\n\n\\[\n= (-48 + 124) + (-86 + 28) = 76 - 58 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
